    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 409,
   "text": "Some examples of applications and experiences that you can build using this SDK\ninclude multiplayer gaming, seamless switching between devices in productivity\napps, and group food ordering.\nWhen developing the Cross device SDK, we followed three basic principles to\ncreate an abstraction layer that safely and respectfully accelerates the\ndevelopment of multidevice apps and experiences. Those princi",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 2,
    "repeats": 2,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 758,
    "height": 112,
    "widthFraction": 0.59,
    "leftFraction": 0.23,
    "pageFraction": 0.18,
    "aboveFold": true
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 15,
   "tag": "ul",
   "landmarks": [
    "section",
    "section",
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 304,
   "text": "Ubiquitous: The SDK should work on every device possible, starting with\nphones and tablets.\nModular: Developers should be able to mix the SDK with other solutions.\nEmpowering: The SDK does not restrict you to specific cross-device\nexperiences, but rather lets you build your own features and experiences.",
   "counts": {
    "links": 0,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
